        "studs": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "1. Diamond Studs — The Foundation of Every Fine Jewelry Collection",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "heading_font_size": 36,
            "subheading": "NON-NEGOTIABLE FIRST PIECE",
            "subheading_text_color": "#8b7d4a",
            "subheading_background": "#f5f2eb",
            "rich_text": "<p>Diamond studs are the single most versatile piece of jewelry a woman can own. One high-quality diamond per ear, set in solid gold — they work with everything from a white shirt and jeans to a black dress at a formal dinner. Unlike trend earrings that date themselves within a season, a well-made pair of diamond studs looks exactly as right in twenty years as it does today.</p><p>The key details that matter: solid 14K gold (not plated), a four-prong setting that maximises light return, and a stone size that reads as intentional rather than minimal. Lab diamond studs offer the same brilliance as mined at a price point that makes it easier to size up — a 0.5ct to 1ct total weight is the sweet spot for everyday wear.</p><p>Our <a href=\"https://www.milanojewelry.com/products/classic-round-4-prong-lab-diamond-studs?variant=40716972195973\"><em>Classic Round 4-Prong Diamond Studs</em></a> are the purist's choice — the definitive version of this piece. The <a href=\"https://www.milanojewelry.com/products/oval-lab-diamond-huggie-hoop-earrings\"><em>Oval Lab Diamond Huggie Hoops</em></a> are the modern alternative if you prefer something that sits closer to the ear with a little more contemporary presence.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/KE-1835-W3.jpg",
            "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/KE-2419-W3.jpg",
            "products_heading": "Featured pieces:",
            "product_list": [
              "classic-round-4-prong-lab-diamond-studs",
              "oval-lab-diamond-huggie-hoop-earrings"
            ],
            "accent_text": "",
            "accent_text_color": "",
