        "bracelet": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "4. A Tennis Bracelet — The Wrist Piece That Works Everywhere",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "heading_font_size": 36,
            "subheading": "UNIVERSALLY FLATTERING ",
            "subheading_text_color": "#8b7d4a",
            "subheading_background": "#f5f2eb",
            "rich_text": "<p>The tennis bracelet is the piece that fashion cycles around without ever replacing. It works equally well with a blazer, a bikini, and a wedding guest dress — worn slightly loose on one wrist, alone, with nothing else competing for attention. It is the definition of an investment jewelry piece: classic setting, real stones, endlessly wearable.</p><p>The tennis bracelet earned its name in 1987 when Chris Evert stopped a US Open match to search for her diamond bracelet after it snapped off her wrist mid-play — and the name has stuck ever since. That's the kind of cultural staying power that separates an investment piece from a trend piece.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.milanojewelry.com/products/classic-lab-diamond-tennis-bracelet?pr_prod_strat=e5_desc&pr_rec_id=c17afbdc1&pr_rec_pid=7095967318149&pr_ref_pid=7231849496709&pr_seq=uniform\">Classic Lab Diamond Tennis Bracelet in 14K gold</a> is the purist's version — the piece as it was meant to be worn. The <a href=\"https://www.milanojewelry.com/products/oval-bezel-lab-diamond-tennis-bracelet\">Oval Bezel Lab Diamond Tennis Bracelet</a> is the contemporary alternative: a low-profile bezel setting that sits flat against the wrist and suits those who prefer a more modern silhouette.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/KB1627-W1_622948b3-f0b3-4cf2-b80a-ef7fe8dd554b.jpg",
            "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/70623FGYG-OV_SGTVEW_ENLRES.jpg",
            "products_heading": "Featured pieces:",
