          "settings": {
            "title": "What is investment jewelry?",
            "answer": "<p>Investment jewelry refers to fine jewelry pieces made from precious metals and genuine stones that retain value and relevance over decades. Unlike fashion jewelry, investment pieces are built to be worn daily and passed down.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q4": {
          "type": "faq_question",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Should I buy lab-grown or natural diamonds?",
            "answer": "<p>Both lab-grown and natural diamonds are real diamonds with identical physical and optical properties. Lab-grown diamonds offer exceptional value and are an excellent choice for everyday fine jewelry. Natural diamonds carry traditional rarity and resale associations that matter to some buyers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q5": {
          "type": "faq_question",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I build a fine jewelry collection on a budget?",
            "answer": "<p>Start with one versatile piece you'll wear daily — diamond studs or gold hoops — and add one piece per year or per milestone. Prioritize solid gold settings and quality stones over quantity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q6": {
          "type": "faq_question",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "What metal is best for everyday jewelry?",
            "answer": "<p>14K gold is the standard for everyday fine jewelry — durable enough for daily wear while maintaining rich color. 18K gold is softer and better suited to occasional wear or pieces that won't take daily impact.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q7": {
          "type": "faq_question",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "How should I care for fine jewelry?",
            "answer": "<p>Store pieces separately to prevent scratching, remove jewelry before swimming or exercising, and have settings checked annually by a jeweler. Clean with warm soapy water and a soft brush for most gold and diamond pieces.</p>"
          }
        },
